4.4 Defense-in-Depth Processing Pipeline
Client-provided MIME types, extensions, and file headers are treated as completely untrusted.
Signed PUT URL Constraints:
Header binding requires X-Goog-Content-Length-Range: 1,52428800 (Enforcing a strict 50 MB ceiling at the storage boundary).
Multi-Stage Processing (Cloud Run Worker):
Stage 1: Magic-Byte Sniffing: Checks file signatures (e.g., MP4 ftyp, WebP RIFF....WEBP). Magic-byte matching is a preliminary sanity check, not proof of safety.
Stage 2: Codec & Container Inspection: Decodes bitstreams using sandboxed FFprobe/libavcodec. Enforces container specs (max 1080p, max 60s duration, valid AAC/H.264 streams). Rejects polyglots and malformed atom structures.
Stage 3: Local Sandboxed Malware Scan: Scanned using an isolated, containerized ClamAV daemon. Zero files or PII are transmitted to external multi-tenant scanning APIs (e.g., VirusTotal Public), upholding Philippine Data Privacy Act compliance.
Stage 4: Metadata Scrubbing: Strips all EXIF, GPS, camera serials, and XMP metadata chunks.
