5.2 Passkey Multi-Device Sync Counter Handling
Under WebAuthn Level 3 specifications, synced passkeys (e.g., Apple iCloud Keychain, Google Password Manager) do not increment monotonic hardware signature counters and frequently report signCount = 0.
Enforcement Rule:
If stored signCount == 0 and received signCount == 0: Allowed (Recognized as synced multi-device credential).
If stored signCount > 0 and received signCount > storedSignCount: Allowed (Monotonic hardware authenticator; update stored count).
If stored signCount > 0 and received signCount <= storedSignCount: REJECTED (Hard Replay Attack Detection).
